    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A sultanate founded by Turkic slave soldiers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samanid-empire">Samanids</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazni">Ghazni</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, Khurasan and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a> (r. 998–1030) led repeated raids into northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, sacking the temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somnath-temple">Somnath</a> in 1026.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> took Khurasan at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dandanaqan">Dandanaqan</a> in 1040; the Ghurids burned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazni">Ghazni</a> and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore">Lahore</a> in 1186.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The scholar al-Biruni, brought to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazni">Ghazni</a> after Mahmud conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a>, learned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> and wrote a detailed study of Indian religion, science and customs, completed around 1030.</p></aside>
    </section>

